#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""kith-migrate — move this Mac from the hq names to Kith's, and back.

  kith migrate run [--dry-run]   print every step; then back up ~/.hq, move it into ~/.kith (~/.hq becomes a link), add
                             ~/kith beside ~/hq, repoint the kith/hq commands, replace the dev.hq.* background jobs by
                             dev.kith.*, switch the Claude Code plugin to kith@kith and rewrite ~/.hq paths in settings
  kith migrate run --undo        reverse it from the manifest (~/.kith/migrate-manifest.json) and the backup
  kith migrate run --force       go on although an agent run, a scheduled run or kith ask is active
  kith migrate run --status      where it stands (kith doctor says the same)

Cutover of a module to the Kith core (the framework in core/runtime/src/cutover/; no module registers one yet):
  kith migrate step MODULE [--dry-run] [--force]   snapshot, import, same-answer check, switch, tombstone the old files
  kith migrate status                              each module's state
  kith migrate check MODULE                        the same-answer check on its own
  kith migrate rollback MODULE [--force]           export back (also: kith rollback MODULE); refuses while a claim is live

Safe to run again: a finished migration is a no-op, a stopped one continues. The backup ~/.kith-migrate-backup-<time>/ is
never deleted. Details: kernel/lib/kith_migrate.py, docs/moving-from-hq.md.
"""
import os, sys

sys.path.insert(0, os.path.join(os.path.dirname(os.path.realpath(__file__)), '..', 'lib'))
import kith_migrate  # noqa: E402

if __name__ == '__main__':
    sys.exit(kith_migrate.main(sys.argv[1:]))
